Read-only plan review. Do not edit files or mutate repo state.

Context: We investigated a Trails UI dirty PR issue in entirehq/entire.io. Root cause: active trails store `repo_trails.base`, but linked GitHub PRs can target a different base in stacked PR workflows. Current update/merge/mergeability/checks paths use stored `row.base`, so updating a stacked PR trail may merge `main` into the branch even though the backing PR targets a stack branch, leaving GitHub PR mergeability dirty. Evidence: PR #1417 in entireio/cli is `tokens-profile -> tokens-agent-brief`, while captured trail #559 had base `main`. Code inspected: `api/src/lib/auto-trails.ts`, `api/src/lib/webhook/processing.ts`, `api/src/lib/trail-ci.ts`, `api/src/lib/github.ts`, `api/src/routes/trails.ts`, `api/src/lib/trail-base.ts`. Open related work: trail gates stack #2445/#2501/#2502/#2503 introduces an up-to-date gate that appears to use stored base via `resolveBaseBranch`; #2442 is checks-only; #2493 uses base for session filters; #2506 timeline range is merged and separate.

Draft plan to review:
1. Add a shared effective base resolver for active trails. It should use a linked open same-repo PR’s current `base.ref` when `gh_pr_id` exists, the PR head ref matches `trail.branch`, and the trail is not terminal; otherwise fallback to `resolveBaseBranch(row, repo)`. Extend `getPullRequestState` to return `head.ref`, `base.ref`, and repo IDs/names needed to validate same-repo and branch match.
2. Sync stored active trail base from same-repo PR webhooks: on PR `opened`/`ready_for_review`, update existing trail metadata with `{ gh_pr_id, base: pr.base.ref }` when head branch matches and status is active. On PR `edited` with `changes.base`, update the linked active trail where `gh_pr_id === pr.number` and head branch still matches. Keep fork PRs ignored. Do not mutate merged/closed trails.
3. Use effective base consistently in active-trail operations: mergeability endpoint, checks endpoint comparison, merge preflight and merge-base capture, update-branch merge direction/message, CI PR lookup/create, active code-changes/compare paths, and gate up-to-date input gathering. Terminal trails keep snapshot refs / historical behavior.
4. Keep display/API `trail.base` as stored target branch, but because webhooks sync it, UI compare/code overview/session filtering will normally be correct. Do not introduce a public `effective_base` field unless needed by tests or unresolved UI races.
5. Tests: webhook PR open links existing trail and updates base; PR edited base retarget updates linked active trail; terminal/fork/head-mismatch cases do not update; `ensureAutoTrailForBranch` or PR link path does not leave existing trail stale; mergeability/update-branch/checks/merge use linked PR effective base when stored base differs; gate up-to-date uses effective base; CI PR lookup does not create shadow PR against stale stored base; no-checks PR #2442 behavior remains intact.

Please critique this plan for correctness, missing code paths, overreach, and interactions with the open trail gates/checks/timeline PRs. Return concise findings ordered by severity, then any suggested amendments. Do not implement anything.

